    {
      "id": "claim_fbcb1f9ea1ee4b01a15a6ee9e6b5b04a",
      "statement": "Since v0.4.0 every proxied cell call rides a pooled per-peer h1-upgrade tunnel carrying literal HTTP driven by hyper on both ends so byte-faithful headers cross as data, with reserved x-cells-* control headers overwritten by node A and stripped by node B to block header smuggling in either direction.",
